{% block bodyContent %}
<h2 id="plan-who-you-need-to-recruit">Plan who you need to recruit</h2>
<p>Recruit participants whose experiences are relevant to what you need to learn. Aim for a range of behaviours, needs and circumstances, including people who may face barriers or be excluded from the service.</p>
<p>Start with your research questions and define the behaviours, experiences or circumstances participants need to have. Write a recruitment brief that explains the research, what taking part involves and how you will use the findings.</p> 
<p><a href="https://www.gov.uk/service-manual/user-research/write-a-recruitment-brief">Read about writing a recruitment brief (GOV.UK service manual)</a></p>

<h2 id="recruit-a-diverse-range-of-participants">Recruit a diverse range of participants</h2>
<p>Include people with different:</p>
<ul>
    <li>backgrounds</li>
    <li>circumstances</li>
    <li>access needs</li>
    <li>levels of confidence using services</li>
</ul>
<p>Do not rely only on people who are easiest to reach or on the same recruitment source each time. Review who is taking part and adjust your approach if important experiences are missing.</p> 
<p><a href="https://www.gov.uk/service-manual/user-research/find-user-research-participants">Read about finding user research participants (GOV.UK service manual)</a></p>

<h2 id="choose-how-to-find-participants">Choose how to find participants</h2>
<p>Use routes that are appropriate for the people you need to reach, such as:</p>
<ul>
    <li>existing contacts or panels</li>
    <li>community organisations</li>
    <li>specialist recruiters</li>
    <li>recruitment in relevant settings</li>
</ul>
<p>You may need to combine approaches.</p>
<p>Check that participation is voluntary and monitor whether each route is producing the range you need.</p>
<p><a href="https://design.homeoffice.gov.uk/user-research/participant-recruitment">Read about participant recruitment (Home Office user-centred design manual)</a></p>

<h2 id="make-it-possible-for-everyone-to-take-part">Make it possible for everyone to take part</h2>
<p>Ask participants what they need and offer accessible information, flexible ways to respond and reasonable adjustments. Consider:</p>
<ul>
    <li>language</li>
    <li>literacy</li>
    <li>technology</li>
    <li>travel</li>
    <li>session times</li>
    <li>caring responsibilities</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="screen-and-communicate-responsibly">Screen and communicate responsibly</h2>
<p>Use a short screener to confirm essential criteria and create the mix you need. Ask only for information with a clear purpose and protect it appropriately.</p>
<p>Explain what taking part involves. Make sure information about arrangements, incentives and contact details is clear, and tell people promptly if plans change.</p>
